 "method": "All values are rel_absmax (max|a-r|/max|r|, float64; docs/format.md section 2 metric). cuda-fp32: engine GPU fp32 vs cpu-fp32-pyg; reference cuda-fp32-triton is bitwise deterministic (spread 0), so tol = max(1e-5, 3 x the reference's own cuda-vs-cpu rel_absmax) per key; keys no GPU op touches (in.*, enc.x_*) get 1e-6. cuda-fp16: engine fp16-autocast vs cpu-fp32-pyg, tol = 1.75 x the reference fp16's own rel_absmax vs CPU (rounded up, 2 sig. digits): an independent fp16 implementation has the same error mechanism and magnitude but different roundings; the max over ~1e7 elements is a stable statistic, so roughly +-30% implementation variability is expected, and 2x would already hide a mis-placed fp16/fp32 cast; 1.75 keeps headroom without that. 'cuda-fp16-vs-ref-fp16': engine fp16 vs reference cuda-fp16-triton directly, tol = 2 x the reference fp16-vs-fp32-GPU difference (two independent roundings add, worst case 2x). Exact keys (fp32 input assembly) 1e-6. proc.*/latent/dec.* are fp16 tensors in the reference under autocast (stored upcast to fp32); out.pre_bound/out.norm/out.y are fp32. Generated by python/reference/calibrate_tolerances.py from the compare files listed under 'sources'.",
